  "narrative": "For a high apartment in Abdoun (~175 m²), the recommended launch price is 966 JD/m², within a defensible range of 628–1304 JD/m² (confidence: M, 0.52; 80% interval 628–1304). This is anchored on 12 comparable listing(s), each normalised to the subject with market-derived adjustments and calibrated from asking to transaction level; comps needing fewer/smaller adjustments carried more weight. To stay representative of the whole submarket, the comp value was reconciled toward the robust median of all same-type sales (~1071 JD/m² asking) by statistical precision, so a dense pool anchors the price level while the comps supply the subject-specific adjustments. Cross-checks: cost floor ≈ 175, income ceiling ≈ 1054. Convergence supports the estimate; divergence is captured in the risks. Future signals (development score 0.528) justify holding the launch toward the top of the range and raising — never cutting — later. Key risk: Adjusted comps vary 50% — the submarket is heterogeneous.",
